# CODEOWNERS — automatically requests reviews from owners of changed paths.
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Rules:
#   - Syntax: <pattern> @username @org/team (+email addresses work too)
#   - Later rules take precedence over earlier rules for matching files.
#   - Patterns follow the same rules as .gitignore, but are anchored to the
#     repository root and always match (a leading "/" makes anchoring explicit).
#   - Files can have multiple owners; all matching owners are requested.
#   - Keep patterns sorted from general to specific — the LAST match wins.

#######################################
# Default — everything not matched below
#######################################

*                       @JackSmack1971

#######################################
# Repository meta and automation
#######################################

/.github/                @JackSmack1971
/.github/workflows/      @JackSmack1971
/.gitignore              @JackSmack1971
/CODEOWNERS              @JackSmack1971

#######################################
# Documentation
#######################################

/docs/                  @JackSmack1971
*.md                    @JackSmack1971
/README.md              @JackSmack1971

#######################################
# Core source directories
# Replace these example mappings with your real layout.
#######################################

/src/                   @JackSmack1971
/src/core/              @JackSmack1971
/src/api/               @JackSmack1971
/src/cli/               @JackSmack1971

#######################################
# Configuration and deployment
#######################################

/config/                @JackSmack1971
/docker*                @JackSmack1971
/deploy/                @JackSmack1971
/infra/                 @JackSmack1971

#######################################
# Tests
#######################################

/tests/                 @JackSmack1971
**/*_test.*             @JackSmack1971
**/test_*.py             @JackSmack1971

#######################################
# High-risk files — require senior review
#######################################

/security/              @JackSmack1971
**/Dockerfile            @JackSmack1971
/package.json            @JackSmack1971
/requirements*.txt       @JackSmack1971
/CHANGELOG.md            @JackSmack1971
/LICENSE                 @JackSmack1971

#######################################
# Individual file example
#######################################

# A single critical file with an individual owner:
#/src/bootstrap.py       @octocat

#######################################
# Notes
#######################################
# 1. If a file matches multiple rules, only the owners from the LAST matching
#    rule are requested — there is no merging of rules.
# 2. If a team is in an organization, prefix it: @org/team-name. Teams must
#    have visible membership for CODEOWNERS to work.
# 3. Escape special characters in filenames using \ before the character.
# 4. Uncomment and adapt the example rules above to your repository layout.
